# Search Rails API before helpers

Before adding anything under `app/helpers/`, search https://api.rubyonrails.org/ for this app's Rails version (8.1.3.1). Prefer the framework helper. Domain conversion (cents to dollars) stays at the call site.

Money is integer cents (`amount_cents`, `monthly_price_cents`). Rails formats major units, not cents. There is no cents-specific money type or helper. Divide by `100.0`, then format.

Relevant APIs: ActionView `number_to_currency` (delegates to `ActiveSupport::NumberHelper#number_to_currency`), and `Numeric#to_fs(:currency)`.

```ruby
# bad
def format_money(cents)
  format("$%.2f", cents.to_i / 100.0)
end

# in a view
<%= format_money(invoice.amount_cents) %>
```

```erb
<%# good %>
<%= number_to_currency(invoice.amount_cents / 100.0) %>
```

Do not wrap `number_to_currency` in another helper. Do not add a Money gem for display.
